The fault is in `ts-config-service`: its own database calls are slow, and that delay travels up through seat, travel, route-plan and preserve to the dashboard. Nothing else in the telemetry shows a second fault that reached users.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-config-service",
      "fault_kind": "database_call_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.5)/1e6 med_ms, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-config-service' AND span_name IN ('SELECT ts.config','SELECT Config','GET /api/v1/configservice/configs/{configName}') GROUP BY 1", "claim": "Config's own DB span 'SELECT ts.config' has p95 about 2.3 s abnormal, versus about 2.9 ms normal."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration, 0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-config-service' AND span_name IN ('SELECT ts.config','SELECT Config') GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Normal period config DB spans run at roughly 2-4 ms p95, so the slowdown is new."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, service_name, avg(value) v, max(value) mx FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name IN ('mysql','ts-config-service') AND metric IN ('k8s.pod.cpu.usage','k8s.pod.memory.working_set') GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Config and mysql CPU and memory stay low, so no container saturation explains the delay."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_source, attr_destination, metric, avg(value) v, max(value) mx FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE metric='hubble_flows_processed_total' AND attr_source LIKE '%config%' AND attr_destination LIKE 'ts1/mysql%' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Config-to-mysql connection shows no drops and a similar flow count, so the network is not the cause."}
      ]
